  "question": {
    "text": "Borazine, also known as inorganic benzene, can be prepared by the reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-equivalents of &quot;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&quot; with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>-equivalents of &quot;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>&quot;. &quot;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&quot; and &quot;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>&quot;, respectively are",
